  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Introducing a Quality Control System for a motorcycle assembly plant in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Koneksie B.V., also known as Kibo Motorcycles, is a Dutch social enterprise that developed a motorcycle for the African market with the aim to provide safe and reliable transport for all. Through a DGGF-loan Kibo has invested in a motorcycle assembly plant in Kenya. To minimise risks of the investment and to improve local production capacity, Technical Assistance was provided for the introduction of a Quality Management System. This involved the development and implementation of quality management measures for Kibo&#x2019;s 3 key processes: Assembly, Supply Chain and After Sales Services. It also involves the set-up of a Kibo Academy to enable continuous quality improvement and on the job training of staff according to European standards. The project is ongoing and aims to provide sustainable knowledge transfer to at least 12 local employees.</narrative>
  </description>
